# Frontend Structure

These rules apply to `frontend/src/`. Follow them when adding or moving files. Do not dump extra files into an existing page or component folder.

## 1. One folder per page, one folder per component

Pages live under `Pages/`. Components live under `Components/`. The folder name is PascalCase and equals the exported component name.

```text
# BAD
Pages/Journal/Journal.jsx
Pages/Journal/JournalHistory.jsx

# GOOD
Pages/Journal/Journal.jsx
Pages/JournalHistory/JournalHistory.jsx
```

## 2. Allowed files in a page or component folder

A folder contains `<Name>.jsx`, `<Name>.css`, and `<Name>.test.jsx` (or `.test.js`) when tests exist. Nothing else.

```text
# BAD
Pages/Journal/journalImage.js
Pages/Journal/summaryLoadingQuotes.js

# GOOD
Pages/Journal/Journal.jsx
Pages/Journal/Journal.css
Pages/Journal/Journal.test.jsx
```

Page-private assets that are not JS/CSS (for example Lottie JSON) may sit in a subfolder of that page, matching `Pages/Course/unblockAnimation/`.

## 3. Page vs component

A page is routed in `App.jsx`. Anything rendered by two or more pages belongs in `Components/`.

```text
# BAD — shared UI living next to one of its callers
Pages/Journal/JournalConfirmModal.jsx

# GOOD
Components/JournalConfirmModal/JournalConfirmModal.jsx
```

A component used by only one page still belongs in `Components/` once it is a distinct UI unit with its own styles (modals, banners, loading screens). Do not keep it as a second `.jsx` file inside the page folder.

## 4. Styles stay with their owner

A `.jsx` file imports only its sibling `.css`. Never import a stylesheet from another folder. Only app-wide primitives belong in `index.css`: fonts, CSS variables, overlays, and shared animations.

```javascript
// BAD
import '../Journal/Journal.css';
import '../../Pages/ThoughtsTest/TestLoadingScreen.css';

// GOOD
import './JournalHistory.css';
```

## 5. CSS class names match the owning component

Prefix classes with the owning component name so ownership is visible from the class alone. Do not reuse another component's prefix. If two screens share a look, copy the rules into the owner's stylesheet and rename them, or extract a real shared component.

```html
<!-- BAD — JournalSummary borrowing JournalHistory classes -->
<header class="journal-history__header">

<!-- GOOD -->
<header class="journal-summary__header">
```

Shared layout that is truly global (today: `.journal-page` and `.journal-page__main`) may live in `index.css`. Page-specific modifiers of that shell (`.journal-page__main--history`, `.journal-page--history`) stay in the page stylesheet.

## 6. Non-React modules do not live in page folders

| Kind | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Pure helpers | `src/utils/` |
| Static content and config | `src/data/` |
| HTTP client | `src/api/` |
| React context | `src/Context/` |

```text
# BAD
Pages/Journal/journalImage.js
Pages/Journal/summaryLoadingQuotes.js

# GOOD
utils/journalImage.js
data/summaryLoadingQuotes.js
```

## 7. Tests colocate with their subject

Place `<Name>.test.jsx` or `<Name>.test.js` next to the file under test. Do not collect tests in a separate tree.

```text
# GOOD
utils/journalImage.js
utils/journalImage.test.js
Pages/Journal/Journal.jsx
Pages/Journal/Journal.test.jsx
```

## 8. Hard stop

If a change would add a second page-level `.jsx` to an existing page folder, create a new folder instead. Do not "just put it next to the other journal files."
